<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Crannon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">322 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war">Lamian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Crannon was fought in 322 BCE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> between the Macedonian armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antipater">Antipater</a> and Craterus and the Greek allies led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolians">Aetolians</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonians</a> won a limited victory, but the Greek coalition broke up as cities made separate peace. Athens was forced to accept a Macedonian garrison and an oligarchic constitution, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war">Lamian War</a>.</p></div>
